         const FORCED_ISOLATION = 1 << 2;
+        /// Zen: a large stacking context whose opacity is changing (animated on
+        /// the compositor or restyled by script). If its only effect is that
+        /// opacity and it is at the root of the stacking context tree, WebRender
+        /// gives its contents a picture-cache slice of their own and applies the
+        /// opacity when compositing that slice, instead of re-rasterizing the
+        /// tiles under it each time the opacity changes.
+        const OPACITY_GROUP_CANDIDATE = 1 << 3;
+        /// Zen: the transform of this stacking context's reference frame is being
